{"schema_version":"1.0","language":"en","edition":"en-ak","revision":"0","book":{"position":18,"code":"JOB","name":"Job","testament":"OT"},"chapter":41,"content":[{"type":"para","marker":"p","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"1","sid":"JOB 41:1"},"Canst thou draw out leviathan with an hook? or his tongue with a cord ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["which"]}," thou lettest down? ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 41:1"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"2","sid":"JOB 41:2"},"Canst thou put an hook into his nose? or bore his jaw through with a thorn? ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 41:2"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"3","sid":"JOB 41:3"},"Will he make many supplications unto thee? will he speak soft ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["words "]},"unto thee? ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 41:3"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"4","sid":"JOB 41:4"},"Will he make a covenant with thee? wilt thou take him for a servant for ever? ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 41:4"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"5","sid":"JOB 41:5"},"Wilt thou play with him as ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["with"]}," a bird? or wilt thou bind him for thy maidens? ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 41:5"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"6","sid":"JOB 41:6"},"Shall the companions make a banquet of him? shall they part him among the merchants? ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 41:6"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"7","sid":"JOB 41:7"},"Canst thou fill his skin with barbed irons? or his head with fish spears? ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 41:7"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"8","sid":"JOB 41:8"},"Lay thine hand upon him, remember the battle, do no more. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 41:8"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"9","sid":"JOB 41:9"},"Behold, the hope of him is in vain: shall not ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["one"]}," be cast down even at the sight of him? ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 41:9"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"10","sid":"JOB 41:10"},"None ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["is so"]}," fierce that dare stir him up: who then is able to stand before me? ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 41:10"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"11","sid":"JOB 41:11"},"Who hath prevented me, that I should repay ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["him? whatsoever is "]},"under the whole heaven is mine. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 41:11"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"12","sid":"JOB 41:12"},"I will not conceal his parts, nor his power, nor his comely proportion. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 41:12"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"13","sid":"JOB 41:13"},"Who can discover the face of his garment? ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["or"]}," who can come ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["to him"]}," with his double bridle? ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 41:13"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"14","sid":"JOB 41:14"},"Who can open the doors of his face? his teeth ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["are"]}," terrible round about. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 41:14"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"15","sid":"JOB 41:15"},{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["His"]}," scales ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["are his"]}," pride, shut up together ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["as with"]}," a close seal. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 41:15"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"16","sid":"JOB 41:16"},"One is so near to another, that no air can come between them. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 41:16"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"17","sid":"JOB 41:17"},"They are joined one to another, they stick together, that they cannot be sundered. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 41:17"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"18","sid":"JOB 41:18"},"By his neesings a light doth shine, and his eyes ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["are"]}," like the eyelids of the morning. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 41:18"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"19","sid":"JOB 41:19"},"Out of his mouth go burning lamps, ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["and"]}," sparks of fire leap out. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 41:19"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"20","sid":"JOB 41:20"},"Out of his nostrils goeth smoke, as ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["out"]}," of a seething pot or caldron. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 41:20"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"21","sid":"JOB 41:21"},"His breath kindleth coals, and a flame goeth out of his mouth. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 41:21"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"22","sid":"JOB 41:22"},"In his neck remaineth strength, and sorrow is turned into joy before him. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 41:22"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"23","sid":"JOB 41:23"},"The flakes of his flesh are joined together: they are firm in themselves; they cannot be moved. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 41:23"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"24","sid":"JOB 41:24"},"His heart is as firm as a stone; yea, as hard as a piece of the nether ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["millstone. "]},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 41:24"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"25","sid":"JOB 41:25"},"When he raiseth up himself, the mighty are afraid: by reason of breakings they purify themselves. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 41:25"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"26","sid":"JOB 41:26"},"The sword of him that layeth at him cannot hold: the spear, the dart, nor the habergeon. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 41:26"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"27","sid":"JOB 41:27"},"He esteemeth iron as straw, ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["and"]}," brass as rotten wood. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 41:27"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"28","sid":"JOB 41:28"},"The arrow cannot make him flee: slingstones are turned with him into stubble. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 41:28"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"29","sid":"JOB 41:29"},"Darts are counted as stubble: he laugheth at the shaking of a spear. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 41:29"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"30","sid":"JOB 41:30"},"Sharp stones ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["are"]}," under him: he spreadeth sharp pointed things upon the mire. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 41:30"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"31","sid":"JOB 41:31"},"He maketh the deep to boil like a pot: he maketh the sea like a pot of ointment. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 41:31"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"32","sid":"JOB 41:32"},"He maketh a path to shine after him; ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["one"]}," would think the deep ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["to be"]}," hoary. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 41:32"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"33","sid":"JOB 41:33"},"Upon earth there is not his like, who is made without fear. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 41:33"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"34","sid":"JOB 41:34"},"He beholdeth all high ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["things:"]}," he ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["is"]}," a king over all the children of pride. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 41:34"}]}]}
